{"amendments":[{"body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs:78-87`, `:536-539`, `:643-657`, and `:702-716`, new juveniles/sub-adults/adults are added by bumping `count` (and sometimes `reserve_g`) only. The destination cohort's `condition_index` and `maturation_accum` are never reset or blended with the incoming animals, even though `update_condition()` already ran earlier in the day. If a stage previously emptied with stale condition or fractional maturation progress, later recruits inherit that extinct cohort state and can be blocked or promoted immediately on the same tick. Reinitialize or count-weight these fields whenever a stage receives entrants, and add a regression test for hatch/promote-after-empty cases.","rationale":"This breaks the stage model's cohort semantics: newly hatched juveniles or newly promoted sub-adults can carry metadata from animals that no longer exist, producing incorrect same-day maturation and stale condition gating."}],"summary":"Reviewed the shrimp stage-model implementation, migration logic, and snapshot surface, then ran `cargo test -p tank_core --test shrimp_population`, `save_load`, and `validation`. One correctness issue remains around stale cohort metadata when a stage is repopulated after being empty."}